ntdll: WINEDEBUG=+tptimer logs thread pool timers and the timer queue thread's rounds (Squark).

A diagnostic, off unless the tptimer debug channel is on. TpAllocTimer logs the module the callback
is in (taking the loader lock before any thread pool lock) and the timer it hands out; tp_set_timer
logs the due time as the program passed it (relative in ms, absolute as ms from now, 0, or NULL for
a cancel), the period and the window; TpReleaseTimer the timer. Once a second the
timer queue thread logs how many rounds it made, which NT timer woke it (relative, absolute, other),
how many rounds had no relative timer pending, how many callbacks it submitted, the number of timer
objects and the pending absolute and relative timers. Off, the thread pays one debug-flag check per
round; submit_expired_timers counts callbacks under timerqueue.cs either way.

Applies with or without 0062.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/threadpool.c b/dlls/ntdll/threadpool.c
